Common Docker Workflow for Spring Boot
1. Build the image/ Build docker image

docker build -t spring-boot-rest-services .
spring-boot-rest-services==> image name
2. Run the container

detached

docker run -d -name spring-app -p 9090:9090 spring-boot-rest-services
9090(container port):9090(application port)
3. If your Dockerfile has a different name
For example:

Dockerfile.dev

then use:

docker build -f Dockerfile.dev -t spring-boot-rest-services .

4. View logs:
docker logs spring-app
Follow logs:
docker logs -f spring-app
5. List running containers:
Running
docker ps
All
docker ps -a
6. Stop the container:
docker stop spring-app
spring-app==> container-id
7. Remove the container:
docker rm spring-app
spring-app==> container-id

  7.1 Force remove:
  docker rm -f <container-id>

8. List Images

docker images
9. Remove the image
   docker rmi spring-boot-rest-services

10. docker compose

docker compose with postgresql

version: '3.8'

services:

  postgres:
    image: postgres:16
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: mydb
      POSTGRES_USER: postgres
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"

  springboot:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    environment:
      SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL: jdbc:postgresql://postgres:5432/mydb
      SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME: postgres
      SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD: password
    depends_on:
      - postgres

    Start:

    docker compose up

    Stop:

    docker compose down
11. Execute Commands Inside Container

docker exec -it <container-id> bash

Or if Bash isn't installed:

docker exec -it <container-id> sh

12. Inspect Container
docker inspect <container-id>

13. Network Example

docker network create spring-network

14. Volume Example

    Create volume:

    docker volume create postgres-data

15. Build Without Cache
docker build --no-cache -t springboot-demo .

16. Tag Image

docker tag springboot-demo:latest springboot-demo:v1

17. Push to Docker Hub

Login:
docker login

Tag:

docker tag springboot-demo username/springboot-demo:v1

Push:

docker push username/springboot-demo:v1

18. Useful Cleanup Commands

Remove stopped containers:

docker container prune

Remove unused images:

docker image prune

Remove everything unused:

docker system prune

Remove everything including volumes:

docker system prune -a --volumes

19. Passing Environment Variables

Suppose your application uses:

spring.datasource.url=${DB_URL}
spring.datasource.username=${DB_USER}
spring.datasource.password=${DB_PASSWORD}

Run:

docker run \
-p 8080:8080 \
-e DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://host.docker.internal:5432/mydb \
-e DB_USER=postgres \
-e DB_PASSWORD=password \
springboot-demo

20. Mount application.properties

docker run \
-p 8080:8080 \
-v $(pwd)/application.properties:/app/application.properties \
springboot-demo \
--spring.config.location=file:/app/application.properties

21. Multi-stage Build (Recommended)

# Build stage
FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21 AS build

WORKDIR /app

COPY pom.xml .
COPY src ./src

RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests

# Runtime stage
FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre

WORKDIR /app

COPY --from=build /app/target/*.jar app.jar

ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]

Build:

docker build -t springboot-demo .



